  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two metallic plates form a parallel plate capacitor. The distance between the plate is &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&#39;. A metal sheet of thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and of area equal to area of each plate is introduced between the plates. What will be the ratio of the new capacitance to the original capacitance of the capacitor?<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/744028d4-eb6b-43d5-9a91-c5d72f62976b-image.png\" style=\"width: 201px; height: 230px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "tSu9n",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PNQPY",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "61hej",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5e6AE",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3e83a4dc-9cdf-4440-8382-7b602355fa3e-image.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 174px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;Before the metal sheet is inserted, capacitance is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></math>.</p><p>After the sheet is inserted, the system is equivalent to two capacitors in series, each of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>A</mi></mrow><mfenced><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>C</mi></math>.<br />The equivalent capacity is now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi></math>.</p><p>The ratio is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
